[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ti:141. Sally's First Train Ride]
[00:00.780] Lesson 141. | 第141課。
[00:03.960] Last week, my four-year-old daughter Sally was invited to a children's party. | 上週,我四歲的女兒薩莉被邀請去參加一個兒童派對。
[00:11.905] I decided to take her by train. | 我決定帶她乘火車去。
[00:15.305] Sally was very excited because she had never traveled on a train before. | 薩莉非常興奮,因為她以前從未坐過火車。
[00:21.765] She sat near the window and asked questions about everything she saw. | 她坐在窗邊,問她所看到的一切問題。
[00:27.890] Suddenly, a middle-aged lady came into our compartment and sat opposite Sally. | 突然,一位中年女士走進我們的車廂,坐在薩莉的對面。
[00:35.420] "Hello, little girl," she said. | “你好,小姑娘,”她說。
[00:39.230] Sally did not answer, but looked at her curiously. | 薩莉沒有回答,只是好奇地看著她。
[00:44.685] The lady was dressed in a blue coat and a large funny hat. | 那位女士穿著一件藍色外套和一頂又大又滑稽的帽子。
[00:50.535] After the train had left the station, the lady opened her handbag and took out her powder compact. | 火車離開車站後,那位女士打開手提包,拿出她的粉餅盒。
[00:59.100] She then began to make up her face. | 然後她開始化妝。
[01:03.115] "Why are you doing that?" Sally asked. | “你為什麼要這樣做?”薩莉問。
[01:07.405] "To make myself beautiful," the lady answered. | “為了讓自己變漂亮,”那位女士回答。
[01:12.520] She put away her compact and smiled kindly. | 她收好粉餅盒,友好地笑了笑。
[01:17.455] "But you are still ugly," Sally said. | “但你仍然很醜,”薩莉說。
[01:22.040] Sally was amused, but I was very embarrassed. | 薩莉覺得好笑,但我卻非常尷尬。